  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this page reads",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Tokens by kind** are the daemon's own counters of each settled session, recorded with `step.cost`: `step.tokens.cache_read`, `step.tokens.cache_write` and `step.tokens.uncached`, which add up to `step.tokens.input`, beside `step.tokens.output`. A kind is counted only where every attempt of the session measured it, so a session before these counters, or on a harness that does not say its cache, adds to the input and to no kind. No dollars by kind: the harness prices a session whole, and no price is kept by hand here.\n\n**Per task**: a task is a step of a run: its tries and its rounds summed, counted once when its first try settles (step.tasks). A mean is the range's cost or tokens over the range's tasks, so a step whose first try settled before the range and a later try inside it adds cost and no task: read a mean over a day or more.\n\n**The quota** is the subscription's windows, `quota.used` (percent) and `quota.resets_at` (seconds since the epoch), set by the daemon at each good reading, every ten minutes, through the one asker the board reads, so an open board adds no ask; after a restart the gauges are absent until the first reading. Its panels show the last seven days, or the last day for the five-hour window, whatever the range picked. **Even pace** is the share of the window that has passed: the used line above it is ahead of an even spend."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Tokens by kind",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
